        ${faa&&faa.toUpperCase()!==String(lab).toUpperCase()?`<div class="muted">FAA: ${esc(faa)}</div>`:""}</td></tr>`;
    }).join("");
    return `<h3>${esc(t)} <span class="muted">${entries.length} codes</span></h3>
      ${note?`<p class="muted">${esc(note)}</p>`:""}
      ${big?`<input class="tf" placeholder="Filter these ${entries.length} codes" oninput="filterTable(this)">`:""}
      <table class="codes">${rows}</table>`;
  }).join("")+
  `<h3>About the airline codes</h3>
   <p class="muted">Operator designators are not in the FAA's SDRS zip. They come from two FAA lists merged: the December 2006 Air Carrier/Operator cross-reference and the current list of certificated 121 and 135 operators. ${OPGAP?`Of the ${num(OPGAP.designators)} designators in this data, ${num(OPGAP.resolved)} resolve, covering ${OPGAP.covered_pct}% of all reports.`:``} Codes issued after 2006, and carriers that merged but kept filing
   under a legacy code, are shown exactly as filed. Always check current ownership before publishing.</p>
   <h3>Where these tables come from</h3>
   <p class="muted">The FAA publishes them as a zip on the SDRS front page, at
   sdrs.faa.gov/Documents/SDRS Look-Up Tables.zip. This is the edition dated July 2026. The
   corrosion grades are not in that zip; they come from FAA Order 8300.12 and EASA IP 119.</p>`;
}
